Patches applied to third-party sources before building.

  qemu-11.0.3.patch   Android/bionic build fixes plus the Limbo integration
                      hooks (shared-library emulator, runtime-tunable display
                      and audio settings). See the header of the file itself,
                      and README.developers in the root directory, for how to
                      apply it.

  sdl2-2.32.4.patch   Limbo's SDL2 changes, forward-ported from 2.0.8. Now
                      only the mouse-warp suppression: SDL gained a native
                      AAudio backend in 2.0.14, which replaces the dlopen
                      bridge the old patch carried.

Removed relative to upstream Limbo:

  qemu-2.9.1.patch    Both hooked into Makefile.target, which QEMU deleted in
  qemu-5.1.0.patch    5.2 when the build moved to meson. Neither version can
                      be built by this tree any more; use upstream Limbo if
                      you need them.

  glib-2.56.1.patch   glib is no longer built with autotools. From 2.58 it is
  android.cache       meson-only, and android-config/build-deps.sh cross-builds
                      glib 2.84 (with libffi/pcre2/proxy-libintl as meson
                      subprojects) without needing either file.
